VERB NOT FOUND — WEB ARCHIVE
============================

An English-parser interactive fiction created for the final morning of EPC
Class 5 at CUHK-Shenzhen in August 2026.

The game engine is written in C. Emscripten compiles the same parser and story
state into WebAssembly; a small React interface supplies the browser terminal.
The published site is entirely static. Commands run locally in the visitor's
browser and are never sent to a server.


PRIVACY
-------

Only questionnaire messages authorized for public sharing are included. Four
private messages remain as sealed game objects, but their bodies, signatures,
recipient names, and original questionnaire metadata are absent from this
repository. Never copy questionnaire_result.csv or epc_info into this repo.


LOCAL BUILD
-----------

Requirements:

  - a C11 compiler
  - Node.js 22.13 or newer
  - Emscripten 6.0.8

Build and verify the C game:

  make test

Build the WebAssembly runtime and site:

  npm install
  make web
  npm run dev

Create the production files:

  make site


GITHUB PAGES
------------

Push this directory as its own repository named verb-not-found. On GitHub,
open Settings -> Pages and choose GitHub Actions as the publishing source.
Every push to main will test the native game, compile WebAssembly, build the
static site, and deploy it.

For the GitHub account tem2021, the expected project URL is:

  https://tem2021.github.io/verb-not-found/


CONTROLS
--------

Commands are short English phrases. Try L, X COMMA, READ MESSAGES, WORDS,
HELP, or HINT. The up and down arrow keys recall previous commands.


ARCHIVE POLICY
--------------

Tag the performance snapshot before making later story changes. Generated
WebAssembly and dist files are intentionally excluded from Git; the pinned
toolchain and workflow rebuild them from the archived C source.
